{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest","id":1446646,"title":"High Wyrd Fairest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-30T13:07:51-07:00","id":1446646,"title":"High Wyrd Fairest","content":"I know there was criticism of my idea of high wyrd Fairest developing alien beauty and I should stick closer to fairest blessing so, the mechanics don't become too confusing and complex. However, I don't want fairest to simply evolve into epic heroic knights in shining armor or fairy princesses. I want them to become the fae creatures whose beauty drives mortal men and women to madness and self destruction, like the Rusalka, Samodiva, Leanan-Sidhe, and Selkies.<br /> <br /> While some fairest would enjoy this power, I can see others feeling a great deal of guilt over the lives they ruin.<br /> <br /> This idea was inspired by Junji Ito's <i>Tomie </i>series and Ed Brubaker Sean Phillip's <i>Fatale </i>series, about a seemingly immortal women who has the power cause men to becomes infatuated with her.<br /> <br /> Here are some edits I mate to my idea for the evolution of the Fairest seeming blessing. I developed the curse with the idea of your seeming become a danger to your mortal/ lower wyrd allies.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Fairest</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Wyrd 7</i></b>: The fairest never suffers social penalties due to appearance or actions. They also always match their audiences ideal of a fairy princess, knight in shining armor, or prince charming.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Wyrd 8</i></b>: All seductions difficulties made against a character who feels or romantic, physical, or simple friendship toward the fairest are zero. By Spending a point of glamor and touching a target, the fairest can roll Manipulation+ Persuasion or Subterfuge + Wyrd against a characters Composure + Wyrd. If successful, the target suffers the Swooned Condition, which evolves into<b><i> Ravished Condition</i></b>.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Wyrd 9</i></b>: The fairest gains 4 automatic successes in all rolls where appearance would help. And any wound that would mar the fairest perfect beauty instantly heals, not leaving a scar.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Wyrd 10: </i></b>Any supernatural power <i>(contracts, disciplines, gifts, spells)</i> that would mentally or emotionally influence the fairest is an automatic dramatic failure.<br /> But Beauty is as much a curse as a blessing.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Wyrd 7: </i></b>Add a dice for a clarity roll when you accidentally cause misfortune towards your allies.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Wyrd 8: </i></b> When the Fairest causes the <b><i>Ravished Condition </i></b>on a mortal or changeling with a Wyrd below 6, they suffer the <b>Bacchanalia <i>Tilt</i></b>.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Wyrd 9: </i></b>Any mortal that gazes on the fairest gains the <b><i>Fae-Struck Condition</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Wyrd 10</i></b>: Gain an automatic derangement.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Ravished Condition: </i></b>The character feels waves of ecstasy so great that they are knocked unconscious. <br /> <br /> <b>Bacchanalia <i>Tilt: </i></b>The ecstasy the character feels are so strong it damages their body. The character suffers seven points of damage.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Fae-Struck Condition: </i></b>The characters feel an all-consuming love for the fairest that overrides self-preservation. They will walk thousands of miles, commit murder, or acts of terrorism just to be near the <i>Fairest</i>.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T13:43:26-07:00","id":1446654,"title":"","content":"Kind of unplayably powerful for my tastes, but just two things stuck out to me anyway for feedback:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest#post1446646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All seductions difficulties made against a character who feels or romantic, physical, or simple friendship toward the fairest are zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a &quot;difficulty?&quot; Did you mean to say they ignore dice penalties on these rolls? You also say Swooned &quot;evolves&quot; into Ravished, but not how or when. Just instantly? What's the point of Ravished being a Condition rather than just saying they suffer Swooned and also are knocked unconscious?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest#post1446646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And any wound that would mar the fairest perfect beauty instantly heals, not leaving a scar.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they're... immune to damage? Or they take damage normally but it just never shows outwardly until they collapse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T16:37:31-07:00","id":1446683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1446654#post1446654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of unplayably powerful for my tastes, but just two things stuck out to me anyway for feedback:<br /> <br /> I think a chronicle featuring a high wyrd fairest should deal with the chaos their beauty causes and how deals with it. Most fairest would not want to develop their wyrd so high because of how powerfully destructive their beauty is, unless they have a major objective in mind. The fairest might also have been someone who was plane as an ordinary mortal. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What is a &quot;difficulty?&quot; Did you mean to say they ignore dice penalties on these rolls? You also say Swooned &quot;evolves&quot; into Ravished, but not how or when. Just instantly? What's the point of Ravished being a Condition rather than just saying they suffer Swooned and also are knocked unconscious?<br /> Yes, and swooned turns into ravished the next turn. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So they're... immune to damage? Or they take damage normally but it just never shows outwardly until they collapse?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They take damage normally from their frailties and cold iron, but all other damage heals instantly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T16:38:19-07:00","id":1446684,"title":"","content":"I think a chronicle featuring a high wyrd fairest should deal with the chaos their beauty causes and how deals with it. Most fairest would not want to develop their wyrd so high because of how powerfully destructive their beauty is, unless they have a major objective in mind. The fairest might also have been someone who was plane as an ordinary mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:43:00-07:00","id":1446698,"title":"","content":"What is a &quot;difficulty?&quot; Did you mean to say they ignore dice penalties on these rolls? Yes, they ignore dice penalties to these rolls.<br /> <br /> You also say Swooned &quot;evolves&quot; into Ravished, but not how or when. Just instantly? What's the point of Ravished being a Condition rather than just saying they suffer Swooned and also are knocked unconscious? Swooned turns into ravished, the next turn. When the character wakes up, they still have the swooned condition, but not the ravished tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:45:06-07:00","id":1446700,"title":"","content":"What I am thinking of doing is, like the <i>Fairest of Them All</i> True Fae title, emphasize that this blessing will not work on a character motivated by true love or true friendship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:49:23-07:00","id":1446702,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Stupid Loserman;n1446654]Kind of unplayably powerful for my tastes, but just two things stuck out to me anyway for feedback:<br /> <br /> <br /> I do agree that a high wyrd fairest is almost brokenly powerful, but I want such a high wyrd fairest chronicle to emphasize how their beauty makes it almost nearly impossible to function in normal society and how such a character tries to adjust.<br /> <br /> I can also see some high wyrd fairest enjoying the chaos they create. I have an idea for Snow White as high duchess of the Ice-bond heart in Germany and a major antagonist in a changeling chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T03:26:21-07:00","id":1446768,"title":"","content":"My primary criticism from the other thread still holds true: This forces a very narrow view on a Seeming on <i>everyone</i> of that Seeming, with little to no room for individualisation. In this case the effects themselves are quite generic so they wouldn't be completely out of place on any individual Fairest, but forcing literally all Fairest to gain and suffer the same advantages and disadvantages means you're forcing all of them to go through the same type of story with the same obstacles and likely to only have a few different outcomes of those stories. Look at what high Wyrd gives you by RAW: Frailties. But you don't get specific Frailties handed to you; you pick the Frailties that lost fits the character.<br /> <br /> If you want to make powerul NPCs to really stand out from regular changelings, I wholeheartedly advice you to <i>personalise</i> their advantages and drawbacks. Design Snow White according to the character she is in your campaign; not according to what you think a poweful Fairest would become.<br /> Take a look at how Entitlements work. Since each is unique, they grant extreme amounts of flavour, and they explain why a character would transform in ways that can't be replicated by others. I'm not saying you should use Entitlements as is, but the concept of adding a &quot;secondary template&quot; on top of characters to make them powerful and stand out makes a whole lot more sense to me than them gaining a bunch of character defining traits from just having a high Wyrd rating. If we compare to Mage, it'd be like having Gnosis 7 automatically turns you into a lesser Archmaster, with each additional dot giving more Archmaster traits.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for my criticism of individual advantages and drawbacks:<br /> I like the removal of social penalties as well as being able to inflict Swooning. It's a lot like Awe from Majesty in VtR, which could be really good inspiration if you own that book.<br /> <br /> I dislike how Swooning turns to Ravished. It's really weird to me that a social power abruptly ends social situations (because the other party literally falls unconscious) and it's way too easy to use to end combat in a way that puts the opponent at a lethal disadvantage.<br /> Speaking of lethality, since 7 health is very average, Bachanallia risks mortally wounding a majority of everyone the Fairest can use this on. This is particularly egregious in combination with the fact that they're also unconscious and can't do anything to stabilise themselves and are left completely defenseless against you or anyone else who wants a piece of them.<br /> Minor nitpick: Ravished and Bachanallia shouldn't be a Condition or a Tilt since they describe instantaneous effects. When you hit a character with a sword you don't give them the Hit by a Sword Tilt which deals [successes + weapon modifier - general armour] damage; you just deal that damage.<br /> <br /> Rather than giving a bonus to all rolls where appearance matters, I'd give them something similar to Striking Looks (but obviously more powerful than the base Merit). It limits when the bonus is applied, but that limit gives some individualisation and thus flavour.<br /> <br /> Instantly healing everything that isn't inflicted by frailties is extremely potent. I think you can come up with something less powerful but still fitting. For example, only healing bashing and lethal damage but not aggravated, and only at the end of their turn (stolen from Werewolf) or give them ridiculous armour ratings against anything that would mar their beauty but not other sources of damage. I.e. the best way to bring down Snow White might be to poison her, although that's quite possibly a Frailty of hers.<br /> <br /> Fae-Struck is tough but fitting. But it does need some work so it doesn't ruin basically all Touchstones.<br /> <br /> Derangements aren't a thing in 2e, thankfully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-01-2021, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:17:59-07:00","id":1446823,"title":"","content":"The way I envision it, your seeming is the identity forced on you by your <i>Keeper. </i>What causes clarity damage as your wyrd get higher and higher is the identity given to you by your <i>Keeper </i>reasserting itself. This is why it makes sense to me that you seeming blessing's evolution would be a bit narrow.<br /> <br /> Your kith on the other hand, represents your own talent/potential, skills, even vices that drew your <i>Keeper </i>to you. You can give your character more individualism through a merit like <b><i>potent kith</i></b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:23:05-07:00","id":1446825,"title":"","content":"A major part of an epic changeling chronicle is the internal struggle between the changeling's TRUE IDENTITY and the identity forced on them by their <i>Keeper.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T15:22:26-07:00","id":1446853,"title":"","content":"I think that makes less sense, imo. It implies all Keepers are trying to form the same six archetypal characters from all of their human victims.<br /> Also, the idea that the role given by the Keeper starts reasserting itself is still fully compatible with individualised advantages and disadvantages. Basically, rather than Snow White being forced into a generic archetype, she gets forced into the specific role her Keeper meant for her.<br /> I can't tell you how to run your game, but I really do think you're doing your game a disservice by developing generic systems that impose limits on how you design your NPCs rather than developing your NPCs directly to make them fit the themes of your game.<br /> Like, imagine that Frailties gained at various Wyrd ratings were predetermined. They're equally as limiting to the characters as personalised Frailties, but having them be predetermined also means they're limiting the way you can design the characters. I don't think you'd gain anything by having predetermined Frailties. That's how I feel about Seeming specific advantages and disadvantages at Wyrd 7+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T15:53:12-07:00","id":1446856,"title":"","content":"I don't envision each seeming being an archetypal role and their will be variance in the Seemings; a fairest can be a knight in shining armor, or a succubus, or a ballerina, a wailing banshee who cleans the clothes of the doomed. But it makes sense to me that their Keeper's would give their fairest incredible beauty to glorify their keepers, and themselves. As the wyrd of the fairest rises, it makes sense to me that their beauty would shine/burn more brightly.<br /> <br /> Some fairest would relish this. Especially if they were plain or even homely as ordinary mortals. Others would feel a great deal of guilt over this and take steps to prevent this from happening. Keeping their wyrd low would be pretty simply, but some fairest would have an objective that required a high wyrd. As such, it would be more difficult, but not impossible to prevent wrecking havoc with their looks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T16:02:32-07:00","id":1446857,"title":"","content":"More thoughts..<br /> <br /> A major theme of <i><b>Changeling: The Lost </b></i> is identity. Regaining the life and identity the True Fae/ Gentry stole from you, while staying out of the clutches of your Keeper.<br /> <br /> A lot of that is literal, such as escaping a huntsman and not falling into the clutches of a loyalist or racketeer.<br /> <br /> But another large part of it is the internal struggle a changeling has with their seeming. At lower levels, it is much easier to avoid.<br /> <br /> But as the changeling's wyrd reaches a certain level, (I say around 7), the internal struggle is given more focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T16:10:03-07:00","id":1446859,"title":"","content":"Or maybe give each Seemings several divergences of high-Wyrd growth? So one Fairest becomes the Beauty, the other the Prince, and yet another the Witch, and so on.<br /> <br /> Then again, this would end up overlapping with Entitlements... which is part of what Tessie was saying, I think.<br /> <br /> Maybe these \u2018Wyrd Evolutions\u2019 are Seeming-bound Entitlements available to any high-Wyrd chageling of the corresponding Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T17:36:39-07:00","id":1446869,"title":"","content":"Entitlements are one of the ways you create your own story/identity. I envision your seeming being an identity given to you by your Keeper. I CAN see you seeming evolving based on the changeling's actions and how it connects to their kith in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T07:15:57-07:00","id":1446971,"title":"","content":"I want to share some of the source material that inspired by idea for the high wyrd fairest to give people an idea of how I envision playing such a character.<br /> <br /> <b>Tomie: Complete Deluxe Edition</b><br /> The complete classic horror series, now available in a single deluxe volume. Murdered again and again, one girl always comes back for more...<br /> <br /> Tomie Kawakami is a femme fatale with long black hair and a beauty mark just under her left eye. She can seduce nearly any man, and drive them to murder as well, even though the victim is often Tomie herself. While one lover seeks to keep her for himself, another grows terrified of the immortal succubus. But soon they realize that no matter how many times they kill her, the world will never be free of Tomie.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Tomie-Complete-Deluxe-Junji-Ito/dp/1421590565/ref=sr_1_1?crid=21C3ROH77MSIY&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=tomie+junji+ito&amp;qid=1619964121&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=Tomie%2Caps%2C225&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\">Tomie: Complete Deluxe Edition (Junji Ito): Ito, Junji: 9781421590561: Amazon.com: Books</a><br /> <br /> <b>Fatale, Book 1: Death Chases Me</b><ul><li>Secrets, lies, horror, lust, and monsters from the time before time all collide in <i>Fatale: Death Chases Me</i>. In present day, a man meets a woman who he becomes instantly obsessed with, and in the 1950s, this same woman destroys the lives of all those who cross her path, on a quest for... what? Ed Brubaker and Sean Phillips' bestselling series will leave you craving more!</li> </ul><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Fatale-Book-Death-Chases-Me/dp/1607065630/ref=sr_1_1?crid=SUC0A8Q18ZEH&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=fatale+ed+brubaker&amp;qid=1619964255&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=Fatale%2Cstripbooks%2C228&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\">Amazon.com: Fatale, Book 1: Death Chases Me (9781607065630): Brubaker, Ed, Phillips, Sean, Stewart, Dave: Books</a><br /> <br /> <b>Fatale, Book 2: The Devil's Business</b><ul><li>In 1970s Los Angeles, Josephine can't hide from the forces of Hollywood, Satanic Cults, and creepy 8mm films collected by wealthy deviants. And when a struggling actor and his wounded friend cross her path, all hell will break loose, leaving ripples that echo all the way to modern time, where Nicolas Lash falls deeper into Josephine's spell.</li> </ul><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Fatale-Book-2-Devils-Business/dp/1607066181/ref=pd_bxgy_img_2/135-2434407-9028937?_encoding=UTF8&amp;pd_rd_i=1607066181&amp;pd_rd_r=5370e372-2f9d-45e3-98dd-769601a5dfae&amp;pd_rd_w=DA9Oa&amp;pd_rd_wg=6vIB5&amp;pf_rd_p=fd3ebcd0-c1a2-44cf-aba2-bbf4810b3732&amp;pf_rd_r=GYXXF5RAJVKH42RNPTGE&amp;psc=1&amp;refRID=GYXXF5RAJVKH42RNPTGE\" target=\"_blank\">Amazon.com: Fatale, Book 2: The Devil's Business (9781607066187): Brubaker, Ed, Phillips, Sean, Stewart, Dave: Books</a><br /> <b>Fatale Volume 3: West of Hell</b><ul><li>From the dark days of the depression, to the middle ages and the old west, these tales of horror and myth and the mystery of the Femme Fatale reveal secrets even our heroine doesn't know about yet. Bold and experimental, this is pulp noir horror at its finest!</li> </ul><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Fatale-3-West-Ed-Brubaker/dp/1607067439/ref=pd_bxgy_img_2/135-2434407-9028937?_encoding=UTF8&amp;pd_rd_i=1607067439&amp;pd_rd_r=b90d8766-fe73-4230-84e2-dccc017ffa37&amp;pd_rd_w=1lWa4&amp;pd_rd_wg=tXpln&amp;pf_rd_p=fd3ebcd0-c1a2-44cf-aba2-bbf4810b3732&amp;pf_rd_r=E5TR9Z35VQWFWPFG34QY&amp;psc=1&amp;refRID=E5TR9Z35VQWFWPFG34QY\" target=\"_blank\">Amazon.com: Fatale Volume 3: West of Hell (9781607067436): Ed Brubaker, Sean Phillips, Dave Stewart, Bettie Breitweiser: Books</a><br /> <b>Fatale Volume 4: Pray For Rain</b><ul><li>Sex, drugs, rock-n-roll, and ritual killers all collide in the strangest and most exciting volume of<i> Fatale </i>yet. A strange woman with no memory stumbles into the lives of a struggling grunge band in mid-'90s Seattle. Is she their muse? Will she save them from &quot;One-Hit Wonder&quot; status? Or will she be something much worse, especially since there's a psycho killer on her trail?</li> </ul><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Fatale-Pray-Rain-Image-Comics/dp/1607068354/ref=pd_bxgy_img_3/135-2434407-9028937?_encoding=UTF8&amp;pd_rd_i=1607068354&amp;pd_rd_r=8c36081e-9867-46be-bbf5-5f7bdd2c5253&amp;pd_rd_w=ND0kl&amp;pd_rd_wg=gi1mM&amp;pf_rd_p=fd3ebcd0-c1a2-44cf-aba2-bbf4810b3732&amp;pf_rd_r=YQMVT9FFF8NRP0PNPEZH&amp;psc=1&amp;refRID=YQMVT9FFF8NRP0PNPEZH\" target=\"_blank\">Amazon.com: Fatale Volume 4: Pray For Rain (Fatale (Image Comics)) (9781607068358): Ed Brubaker, Elizabeth Breitweiser, Sean Phillips: Books</a><br /> <b>Fatale Volume 5: Curse the Demon</b><ul><li>The final book in the epic<i> FATALE </i>saga by Brubaker and Phillips. All the threads have come together, and the mysterious immortal Femme Fatale Josephine has one last chance to escape her fate.</li> </ul><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Fatale-Curse-Demon-Image-Comics/dp/1632150077/ref=pd_bxgy_img_2/135-2434407-9028937?_encoding=UTF8&amp;pd_rd_i=1632150077&amp;pd_rd_r=9927a9ca-6729-4543-90ea-4e4f0db2b6ff&amp;pd_rd_w=1gAIM&amp;pd_rd_wg=PEskI&amp;pf_rd_p=fd3ebcd0-c1a2-44cf-aba2-bbf4810b3732&amp;pf_rd_r=B2PN0XCP4TJ8538K5B1D&amp;psc=1&amp;refRID=B2PN0XCP4TJ8538K5B1D\" target=\"_blank\">Amazon.com: Fatale Volume 5: Curse the Demon (9781632150073): Brubaker, Ed, Phillips, Sean, Breitweiser, Elizabeth: Books</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T07:22:20-07:00","id":1446972,"title":"","content":"Another major source of inspiration was Hayao Miyazaki's <b><i>Spirited Away.</i></b> A major theme is the main heroine, Chihiro, struggling to remember her true name after the witch Yubaba gives her a new identity, Sen. This was a major source of inspiration for the internal struggle high wyrd changeling's have to not forget who they originally were.<br /> <br /> You can watch the full movie here.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mKjRXCI1Ggw\" target=\"_blank\">Spirited Away Full Movie English Dubbed - YouTube</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T07:41:00-07:00","id":1446976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1446972#post1446972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another major source of inspiration was Hayao Miyazaki's <b><i>Spirited Away.</i></b> A major theme is the main heroine, Chihiro, struggling to remember her true name after the witch Yubaba gives her a new identity, Sen. This was a major source of inspiration for the internal struggle high wyrd changeling's have to not forget who they originally were.<br /> <br /> You can watch the full movie here.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mKjRXCI1Ggw&amp;quot;]Spirited</a> Away Full Movie English Dubbed - YouTube[/URL]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, the whole movie really is good Changeling motif.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T18:30:59-07:00","id":1447071,"title":"","content":"I have been trying to consider how to best describe how a changeling's identity is warped and changed and the best comparison is <i><b>Hunter the Reckoning: Fall From Grace</b></i>. As a hunter becomes more successful in the <i>Hunt</i> they are given greater access to greater powers including <i>Divine Edges</i>. However, the price is having the hunter's personality totally rewritten and a divine madness.<br /> <br /> What happens to a changeling is somewhat similar. Their blessing's evolve to almost divine abilities, but the cost is their personality starting to be rewritten to what their <i>Keeper </i>originally desired and their frailties. Some changeling's fight against this, through developing their court mantle AND entitlements, but even here their personality is rewritten to better represent their court and the story they have chosen to represent/entitlement.<br /> <br /> To save a little of their original personality, some Changeling's develop their kiths, which was the quality that first drew their<i> Keeper</i> to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T18:49:10-07:00","id":1447075,"title":"","content":"Sounds a lot like Eldritch Titles/Entitlements!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/entitlements-ctl2-oak-ash-and-thorn/\" target=\"_blank\">Eldritch Titles</a></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Contrary to what many changelings may believe or dread, Wyrd 10 and normal entitlements possesses no inherent path to actually becoming Gentry. A few entitlements, however, are <i>eldritch</i> titles: those that demand higher Wyrd and more ominous or fantastical duties. These may possess such paths, though knowledge about them is not widely known.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T18:55:38-07:00","id":1447076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1447075#post1447075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds a lot like Eldritch Titles/Entitlements!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/entitlements-ctl2-oak-ash-and-thorn/\" target=\"_blank\">Eldritch Titles</a></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Contrary to what many changelings may believe or dread, Wyrd 10 and normal entitlements possesses no inherent path to actually becoming Gentry. A few entitlements, however, are <i>eldritch</i> titles: those that demand higher Wyrd and more ominous or fantastical duties. These may possess such paths, though knowledge about them is not widely known.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, an Eldritch Title is one of the ways tries to create a unique identity for themselves. But The Changeling tends to lose their original personality to the Eldritch title. Or that kind of how they go in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T18:58:05-07:00","id":1447078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1447076#post1447076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...The Changeling tends to lose their original personality to the Eldritch title...</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the feeling that's also (at least a part of) what's happening with the Evolved Seemings here; I guess I must be mistaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T19:06:57-07:00","id":1447080,"title":"","content":"Yes, It is also what is happening with the evolved seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T19:08:42-07:00","id":1447081,"title":"","content":"High Wyrd Changeling's can gain an Eldtritch order to break out of the identity their Keeper, but they still lose who they one were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T00:03:43-07:00","id":1447125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1446869#post1446869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entitlements are one of the ways you create your own story/identity. I envision your seeming being an identity given to you by your Keeper. I CAN see you seeming evolving based on the changeling's actions and how it connects to their kith in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really what I was focusing on when I brought up Entitlements. I merely meant to point at how Entitlements are added on top of the normal Changeling template to evolve the changeling.<br /> <br /> My point about individualising your NPCs is not that <i>they</i> get to choose how they evolve. It's that the Gentry get a lot more room to decide how their former wards evolve.<br /> You mentioned how Fairest could be knights in shining armour, succubi, ballerinas and banshees. I think the best way to go about that is developing &quot;evolved Seeming traits&quot; for the particular archetype the Keeper is going for rather than trying to fit all possible subtypes of a Seeming under a single set of evolved traits. The evolved Fairest traits you've developed works a bit for all four of those subtypes, but they also fail to reinforce anything about those subtypes other than their beauty.<br /> What I would do is:<br /> \u2022 Have the changeling chosen to become a shining knight exude an aura of respect, but be compelled to always act chivalrous.<br /> \u2022 Have the changeling chosen to become a succubus irresistable to look at, but unable to gain Glamour through any means other than Harvesting/Reaping from people.<br /> \u2022 Have the changeling chosen to be a ballerina enchant people through their dance, but also unable to stop dancing whenever they have started.<br /> \u2022 Have the changeling chosen to be a banshee have the most enchanting and/or terrifying voice ever, but unable to ever speak without wailing as loud as they can.<br /> And unlike Entitlements, these roles would be completely forced upon the changelings by their Keepers. It's definitely based on their forced Seemings, but individualised to fit the plans their Keepers had for them specifically instead of all of them developing the exact same evolved traits. Those four Fairest still face the same problem, of being forced into a role their Keeper has chosen for them, but now they have unique challenges to overcome and become a lot more interesting for your players. It also gives <i>you</i> a lot more freedom in designing your NPCs because you'd be able to create a lot more varied conflicts for these NPCs. The one downside is that it's a lot more work this way, but it's work I'd welcome if I were to ST a similar game.<br /> <br /> But this is my last post in this thread because I really do feel like an asshole who's saying &quot;no, bad way of running your game&quot; every time I post about this, but that is not my goal. In the end, you do what you think works best for your game. I'm just writing this last post because I think some of the core points of my position hadn't come across clearly and I just wanted to explain them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T10:39:40-07:00","id":1447229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1447075#post1447075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds a lot like Eldritch Titles/Entitlements!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/entitlements-ctl2-oak-ash-and-thorn/\" target=\"_blank\">Eldritch Titles</a></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Contrary to what many changelings may believe or dread, Wyrd 10 and normal entitlements possesses no inherent path to actually becoming Gentry. A few entitlements, however, are <i>eldritch</i> titles: those that demand higher Wyrd and more ominous or fantastical duties. These may possess such paths, though knowledge about them is not widely known.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>A moment like this makes me wonder if things like TV Tropes statements of books describing high Wyrd changelings becoming True Fae might have been overstated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T10:45:07-07:00","id":1447231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1447229#post1447229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A moment like this makes me wonder if things like TV Tropes statements of books describing high Wyrd changelings becoming True Fae might have been overstated.</div> </div> </div> </div>TvTropes is never a reliable source of information, this is known.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T14:34:24-07:00","id":1447272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1447125#post1447125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not really what I was focusing on when I brought up Entitlements. I merely meant to point at how Entitlements are added on top of the normal Changeling template to evolve the changeling.<br /> <br /> My point about individualising your NPCs is not that <i>they</i> get to choose how they evolve. It's that the Gentry get a lot more room to decide how their former wards evolve.<br /> You mentioned how Fairest could be knights in shining armour, succubi, ballerinas and banshees. I think the best way to go about that is developing &quot;evolved Seeming traits&quot; for the particular archetype the Keeper is going for rather than trying to fit all possible subtypes of a Seeming under a single set of evolved traits. The evolved Fairest traits you've developed works a bit for all four of those subtypes, but they also fail to reinforce anything about those subtypes other than their beauty.<br /> What I would do is:<br /> \u2022 Have the changeling chosen to become a shining knight exude an aura of respect, but be compelled to always act chivalrous.<br /> \u2022 Have the changeling chosen to become a succubus irresistable to look at, but unable to gain Glamour through any means other than Harvesting/Reaping from people.<br /> \u2022 Have the changeling chosen to be a ballerina enchant people through their dance, but also unable to stop dancing whenever they have started.<br /> \u2022 Have the changeling chosen to be a banshee have the most enchanting and/or terrifying voice ever, but unable to ever speak without wailing as loud as they can.<br /> And unlike Entitlements, these roles would be completely forced upon the changelings by their Keepers. It's definitely based on their forced Seemings, but individualised to fit the plans their Keepers had for them specifically instead of all of them developing the exact same evolved traits. Those four Fairest still face the same problem, of being forced into a role their Keeper has chosen for them, but now they have unique challenges to overcome and become a lot more interesting for your players. It also gives <i>you</i> a lot more freedom in designing your NPCs because you'd be able to create a lot more varied conflicts for these NPCs. The one downside is that it's a lot more work this way, but it's work I'd welcome if I were to ST a similar game.<br /> <br /> But this is my last post in this thread because I really do feel like an asshole who's saying &quot;no, bad way of running your game&quot; every time I post about this, but that is not my goal. In the end, you do what you think works best for your game. I'm just writing this last post because I think some of the core points of my position hadn't come across clearly and I just wanted to explain them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of do what you mentioned above through the Changelings kith, which is a refinement of their seeming, as well as the skills that drew the true fae to them.<br /> <br /> The reason I am being so stubborn is that most of my fairest characters were not physically beautiful as mortals (though they did gain strike looks when becoming changelings). A lot of them were plain or even homely like Agatha from <b><i>School For Good and Evil</i></b>. I drew on the popular medieval theme of the <i>HOMELY Woman,</i> in which an incredibly ugly woman gains beauty.<br /> <br /> I drew on the theme that many of my fairest characters were initially very happy with their new good looks, but started to become horrified when their appearance alienated the friends and people they most cared about. Worst, their beauty started to destroy the lives of complete strangers.<br /> <br /> The themes I draw upon are how shallow beauty and fame can actually be and what does it mean to truly love someone?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T08:08:04-07:00","id":1448508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1447231#post1447231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TvTropes is never a reliable source of information, this is known.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently in this case TV Tropes had the right of it? In that Equinox Roads actually did say that Wyrd 10 puts one on the path to becoming True Fae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T08:37:21-07:00","id":1448511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1448508#post1448508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently in this case TV Tropes had the right of it? In that Equinox Roads actually did say that Wyrd 10 puts one on the path to becoming True Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording is a bit murky so I can understand if someone reads the book and gets the idea that reaching Wyrd 10 automatically puts you on the path of becoming a True Fae, but that step is not automatic. Reaching Wyrd 10 puts you on the path just as much as all the previous Wyrd increases. Each time you get one step closer. At Wyrd 10 it's just one more step, but it's still a step just as much as reaching Wyrd 9 is a step, or Wyrd 8 before that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T08:48:17-07:00","id":1448512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1448508#post1448508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apparently in this case TV Tropes had the right of it? In that Equinox Roads actually did say that Wyrd 10 puts one on the path to becoming True Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Points of accuracy does not a reliability make-and it's also missing a lot of details and deliberately skewed to encourage a particular reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T09:04:13-07:00","id":1448513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446646-high-wyrd-fairest?p=1448511#post1448511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording is a bit murky so I can understand if someone reads the book and gets the idea that reaching Wyrd 10 automatically puts you on the path of becoming a True Fae, but that step is not automatic. Reaching Wyrd 10 puts you on the path just as much as all the previous Wyrd increases. Each time you get one step closer. At Wyrd 10 it's just one more step, but it's still a step just as much as reaching Wyrd 9 is a step, or Wyrd 8 before that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be more explicit: Becoming Nightmare is not presented as an optional rule, but it's also not presented as a <i>universal</i> rule. That is to say, every changeling who hits Wyrd 10 does not then start becoming nightmare. It happens to <i>some</i> changelings who &quot;unconsciously open [their] heart[s]&quot; to dreams of Faerie, and never without the player's consent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T12:26:28-07:00","id":1448529,"title":"","content":"One day I'll buy all the Changeling books.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}